WEBVTT

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.270
1909 - End of the Ishbalan Civil War

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.270
1909 - End of the Ishbalan Civil War

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.070
Are you not going back?

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.860
They're going to leave you behind.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.530
A grave of a comrade?

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.320
No, an Ishbalan child.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.370
The body was left abandoned on the side of the road.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Let's go back.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.170
The war is over.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:41.170
Inside my heart, the battle in Ishbal is still not over.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.720
No, I'm sure it never will be.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.890
I'm the one who believed in you and entrusted you with my father's research.

00:00:55.060 --> 00:01:00.190
I'm also the one who chose to enter a military academy, wishing for the well-being of the people.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.530
Even if that brought an outcome that I didn't wish for,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.370
I can't escape from the truth.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.660
I can't compensate for it.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.460
I have a favor to ask of you, Sir Mustang.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.220
Please burn the skin off of my back.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.720
How could I do such a-

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.640
At the very least!

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.520
If I can't compensate for it, then at the very least,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.770
I'd like to destroy this secret to flame alchemy on my back,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.980
in order to ensure that the world will never see another Flame Alchemist.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.820
Could you please do that for me?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:48.740
Please set me free.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.410
Please set me free from what my father burdened me with...

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.290
From alchemy.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.670
Please release me from this.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.050
Please.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.390
I understand.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:17.060
I'll burn it off your back with the least amount of scarring possible.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.700
Thank you, Sir Mustang.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:34.750
The new morning we've finally found

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:34.750
Yatto mitsuketa atarashii asa wa

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.790
is being hampered by the past.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.790
Tsukihi ga jama wo suru

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:44.260
What we chased after wasn't the future,

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:44.260
Mukau saki wa tsugi ja nakute

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.090
but the past so full of remorse.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:48.090
Sugi bakari oikaketa

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:54.560
The ruthless memories won't stop playing;

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:54.560
Nariyamanai yousha nai omoide tachi wa

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.650
they won't be forgiving us for a long time.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.650
Yurushite kuresou nimonai

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.490
It's about now that a teardrop

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.490
Sorosoro kana tesaguri tsukareta hoho wo

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:09.160
beings to roll down my fatigued cheeks.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:09.160
Kattou ga koboreochiru

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:14.410
Will this rain ever stop?

00:03:09.490 --> 00:03:14.410
Ame wa itsuka yamunodeshouka

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:19.630
I've been freezing for a long time.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:19.630
Zuibun nagai aida tsumetai

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.920
Why does the rain continue to fix on me?

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.920
Ame wa doushite boku wo erabuno

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.680
I wonder if it could embrace me.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.680
Tsutsumarete iikana

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.470
Today, the rain falls again;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:34.470
Ame wa yamu koto wo shirazuni

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.690
endlessly it falls knowing no end.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.690
Kyou mo furitsuzukukeredo

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.730
We nestle close to each other to share the warmth

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.730
Sotto sashidashita kasa no naka de

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:56.450
under this umbrella, you gently held out to me.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:56.450
Nukumori ni yorisoinagara

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.610
Beyond the Inferno

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.610
Beyond the Inferno

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.010
What's this about, Lieutenant?

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.430
Who do you think you're pointing a gun at?

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:20.850
Who?

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.270
Don't make me laugh.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:27.690
The Colonel always calls me 'Riza' when we're alone together.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:28.820
Dammit!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.150
So you guys have something going on?!

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.030
Just kidding.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.450
Thanks for falling for it, Envy.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.710
I'm going to need you to die here.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.380
That hurts, you bitch!

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.020
Damn you...!

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.310
You shoot too much!

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.440
I'll turn you into a rag and show you to the Colonel-

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:13.740
Colonel?!

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.140
What do you think you're doing to my irreplaceable subordinate?

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.770
Don't be so reckless, Lieutenant.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.940
I thought I told you I'd take care of him myself.

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.250
How dare a lowly human like you look down on-

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.750
Dammit...!

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:54.170
This again-

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.010
So this is your true form.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.510
You look disgusting.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:06.310
So your name 'Envy' comes from 'jealousy'.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.900
Now I get it.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.730
No...!

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:12.900
Stop...!

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:17.360
Jealousy sure is disgusting.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:20.490
No! I don't want to die!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.080
N-No!

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.200
Get out...

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:24.540
PLACEHOLDER

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.540
Nooo!!!

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.660
...of my sight!

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.670
What's this about, Lieutenant?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.290
That's enough, Colonel.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.880
I'll take care of the rest.

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:39.510
One more blow will do the trick.

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:41.140
Lower your gun.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.970
I cannot consent.

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:44.470
Please put your hand down.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.810
Stop joking!

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:46.680
I'm ordering you to lower your gun!

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:55.190
Fullmetal.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.070
Hand him over.

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:04.030
I'll say it once more.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:06.580
Hand him over.

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:09.580
I refuse.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:26.100
He deserves the worst death possible.

00:08:26.930 --> 00:08:28.470
I refuse.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.060
Hand him over!

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:32.060
If not, I'll set your right arm ablaze along with him!

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.440
Well said!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.020
I'll fight you head-on!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.230
But before we get to that, take a good look in the mirror!

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:42.490
Do you plan on standing at the top of this country with a face like that?!

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.200
That's...

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.160
That's not what you've been working your ass off for, is it?!

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:54.210
A subordinate protects their subordinate, and so forth.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:58.630
That should be possible, even for us puny humans.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.170
Sounds interesting.

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.260
I'm in.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:07.810
I want to see what kind of changes
your naive ideals will bring to this country.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.600
So you're going to let your emotions take over
and descend to the path of a savage.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.480
I guess that's fine.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.020
If you're going to insist on living for revenge, I won't stop you.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.570
Hey!

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.700
I don't have the right to interfere with someone's revenge.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:33.040
I'm just interested to see what kind of world will be created by someone held prisoner by hatred.

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:38.210
I won't let you kill Envy, Colonel.

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:42.260
But still, I don't plan on letting Envy live either.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.840
I'll take care of him.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.970
I...

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:47.640
I finally tracked him down!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.850
I know that!

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:50.220
But...

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:57.560
But what you're about to do isn't for the sake of the country, and it's not for the sake of helping your comrades either.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:00.110
You're trying to dispel your hatred.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.740
That intent alone is gnawing at your heart.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:07.320
You can't fall down that path.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.270
Shoot me if you want.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:45.110
But what will you do after you kill me?

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:51.450
I don't plan on living free and easy.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.080
After this battle is over,

00:10:54.620 --> 00:11:00.670
I plan on taking flame alchemy, an art that brings about madness, to the grave along with my body.

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.510
That won't do.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:13.390
I...

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.100
...can't lose you.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:22.440
What's with this situation, I wonder.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.570
Being scolded by a child,

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:28.910
and being cautioned by a man who had been after my life for revenge.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:34.410
I made you go through something dreadful again.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.540
I'm the biggest idiot in the world.

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.640
I'm sorry.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.070
Are you guys retarded?

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.690
Now you're just sugarcoating your words?

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.490
Are you playing a game of "let's be humane"?

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:11.240
You're making my skin crawl.

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:15.120
Are you humans really that extravagant?

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:18.830
Just do what your instincts tell you!

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:21.670
You haven't forgotten, have you, Colonel Mustang?

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.750
Scar's been after your life!

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.170
If I recall...

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:31.840
...it was also Scar who killed the runt's friend's parents too, right?

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:36.510
Oh yeah, and the chimera made from the girl and the dog from East City!

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:40.480
Wasn't it also Scar who killed them?

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:42.650
And on the other hand, you, Scar!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:47.860
What happened to that hatred you had,
due to so many of your brethren being killed in Ishbal?!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.990
That woman over there got all puffed up from being called the "Hawk's Eye",

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:54.870
and shot to death many of your friends!

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:57.080
This is the greatest chance for all of you!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.540
Come on, just do it!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.450
The cast is assembled!

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:04.330
Hate, cry, kill, be killed, and writhe in agony!

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:05.840
Get down on all fours!

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:11.970
There's no way you pieces of shit can just hold hands and be jolly!

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.260
Come on, puny runt.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.930
Come on, Hawkeye.

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:16.300
Mustang!

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:17.680
Scar!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.980
W-Why?

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:31.320
Hey, why?

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:33.780
Hey. Hey! Hey!

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:36.160
Why is this happening?!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.740
W-Why?!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:41.000
Why the hell?!

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:42.120
Envy.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.500
You're... jealous of humans.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:56.090
Humans are supposed to be a lot weaker than you homunculi,

00:13:56.680 --> 00:14:01.520
but even if they get discouraged after being beaten, and even if they get close to falling down after losing their path,

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.350
they continue to get up and fight.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:06.150
Everyone around them helps them get on their feet.

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:12.190
And you're envious of those humans.

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:15.110
By sacrificing something minor,
you'd be able to save something major.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:18.240
It's a simple concept if you just think about it.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:21.870
Humans can't shoot me if I do this, right?

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:25.410
Well, that's what makes you all human.

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:30.750
But if I'm going to transform, wouldn't it be better to turn into someone young and pretty?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:33.380
Humans are so foolish.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:35.680
They risk their lives for something so futile.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.800
They're human, after all.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:39.510
Humans...

00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:41.850
Humans...

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:49.900
Hey! Stop trying to get away!

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:51.610
Whoa, hang on!

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.780
Idiot! If you force yourself out...!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.280
Ow!

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:58.490
Hold it.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.870
He doesn't have much longer.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.250
This is a disgrace.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:09.210
Being turned into a rag like this...

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.170
Being beaten up by you humans...

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:18.970
Beaten by an existence on the same level as shit...

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:23.970
And to make matters worse,

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:30.100
a brat like you who's shitty even by a human's standards...

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.710
Dammit!

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:52.000
Dammit...!

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.090
Dammit!

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.090
This is a disgrace!

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.470
A disgrace!

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:02.930
I, Envy, am jealous of humans?

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:05.430
I, Envy?!

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:13.150
It's the greatest disgrace...

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:17.740
...to be understood by a brat like you.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:31.040
I don't know how much longer you can get away with sugarcoating your words,

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.090
but do try your best.

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.240
Good-bye...

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:03.820
...Edward Elric.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.340
So he took his own life.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.170
What a coward.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:42.400
His wounds are healing!

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.410
Monster!

00:17:46.990 --> 00:17:49.120
Hey, what the hell is that?!

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.500
Good timing! Lend us a hand!

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.910
What do you mean?

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:56.670
We were ordered to shoot Major General Armstrong!

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:59.170
What?! Major General!

00:17:59.170 --> 00:18:00.460
Even the Major?!

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.760
Yes, good timing.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.260
From here on out, I'm in charge of this squadron!

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:09.260
No questions asked, just lend us a hand for now!

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.600
Whoa, what the hell are those?!

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:19.190
Everyone, duck!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.780
Bullets do nothing against them.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:29.160
Destroy their upper jaws!

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.910
At the very least, they won't be able to bite you to death.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.040
Team up with a partner and take down at least one of them.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:41.000
Show me the courage of the soldiers at Central!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.460
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.170
Umm...

00:18:44.170 --> 00:18:46.220
What am I supposed to be doing again?

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:52.100
Oh, I remember now.

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.350
I need to kill the female general.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.400
I won't let you!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:05.950
You're in the way.

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.910
Only being able to use one arm is a bit...!

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:23.920
Major!

00:19:23.920 --> 00:19:24.840
General!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.130
He's going to get beaten to death!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:29.010
Someone needs to go help him!

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:30.220
Leave him be!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:34.220
There's no way a beating like that could bring my younger brother down, considering the way he trains!

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:39.400
This is...

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:41.310
...the end.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:45.820
Major!

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.000
My shoulder joint is back in!

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.880
That's it!

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:46.210
A collaboration of artistic muscles and artistic alchemy.

00:20:46.380 --> 00:20:49.920
Both excellent and elegant!

00:20:55.720 --> 00:20:56.720
Yes.

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:59.060
The Armstrong Mansion is completely empty.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:03.730
Dammit, so they were building tanks in here?!

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:14.910
This is the battlements of the main gate!

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:15.910
Give me the mission headquarters!

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:19.790
We're under attack by tanks that are presumably from Briggs!

00:21:19.790 --> 00:21:20.700
Mission headquarters!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.710
Don't shout at me!

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:22.670
I can see that for myself!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.000
It doesn't matter! Fire back!

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.290
But the civilians have yet to evacuate!

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.130
The main gate will be down if we were to wait for something like that!

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:30.800
Headquarters!

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:31.920
Contact the main gate artillery squadron-

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.930
Dammit, what's going on?!

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.140
You're going to open fire on the urban area?

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:45.980
I'm going to have you repeat that on the radio too.

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:48.150
You scum...!

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:50.570
That equipment is from Briggs!

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.490
How did you get in here?!

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:58.030
Well, there's a man with a good memory who used to work at Central Headquarters,

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:00.870
and happened to remember this location with pinpoint accuracy.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.120
There was also a person who dug an underground path between here and the urban area,

00:22:04.330 --> 00:22:07.250
all by herself.

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.630
There's no one in this world who could do such a thing!

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:11.960
Oh, but there is.

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:13.510
W-Who?!

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:16.510
If someone were to ask me who I am, I would tell them I'm a housewife.

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:19.220
That's what I usually do, but...

00:22:20.390 --> 00:22:24.350
I guess today, I'll tell you my other occupation.

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:27.190
An alchemist!

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.040
Ever since that day passed,

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.040
Ano hi kara zutto

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:47.380
I promised myself that I'd never cry.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:47.380
Nakanaito kimetekitakedo

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:52.880
But even while I hoarded up the pain,

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:52.880
Itami wo kasanetemo

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:58.010
there was something I couldn't forgive myself for.

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:58.010
Nanika wo yurusezu ni ita

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:01.560
I'll never be able

00:22:59.350 --> 00:23:01.560
Mou modorenai

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:04.100
to return to those days.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:04.100
Ikutsumo no hibi

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:03.810
You're alone?

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:08.940
I'm still powerless.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:08.940
Boku wa mada nanimo dekizuni

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:10.400
I figured you'd bring your sons.

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:14.240
I watch as the shards of memories disappear, one by one;

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:14.240
Kimi no ita kioku no kakera

00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:15.780
It doesn't take very many people to scold a brat who committed a blunder, does it?

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:20.200
memories of when you were still with me.

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:20.200
Mata hitotsu kieteyuku

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.320
The Dwarf in the Flask,

00:23:18.530 --> 00:23:20.320
Homunculus.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:23.290
I long to become

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:23.290
Kyou yori motto

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:25.580
stronger than I am now,

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:25.580
Tsuyoku naritai

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:30.630
Slave Number 23, the man who gave me a part of his body.

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:30.960
so that my voice will eventually reach you.

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:30.960
Kono koe ga itsuka todokuyouni

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:33.380
If the wind happens to stop

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:33.380
Arukitsuzukete

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:35.130
This time, you'll become a part of my body.

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:35.880
in the midst of my long journey,

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:35.880
Kaze ga yandara

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:41.100
I'll look up at the sky in search of you.

00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:41.100
Kimi wo sagashite sora miageruyo

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:48.350
Beyond the daybreak, a ray of light breaks free.

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:48.350
Yoake no saki ni hikari ga sasuyo

00:23:49.020 --> 00:23:53.980
A rainbow spans across the sky.

00:23:49.020 --> 00:23:53.980
Niji ga kakaruyo

00:24:00.650 --> 00:24:04.830
Humans, think about what you must do now.

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:08.290
Think about to whom you must prove yourself to,

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:11.500
and why this is.

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:17.050
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:21.580
Episode 55, The Adults' Way of Life.

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:21.580
The Adults' Way of Life

00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:26.310
Walk forward proudly with your head held high.
